IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 124 and 125 -- INDEMNIFICATION,
-- ADVANCES, INSURANCE AND REMUNERATION. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another piece is a plain input and says so.

§ `s 124 Indemnification`

DECLARE `Position of the individual under s 124(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a director or officer of the corporation`
    `a former director or officer of the corporation`
    `an individual who acts or acted at the corporation's request as a director or officer of another entity`
    `an individual who acts or acted at the corporation's request in a similar capacity of another entity`
    `none of those`

§§ `s 124(3) Limitation`

-- The conditions on an indemnity; (1), (4) and (5) all refer to them, so they come first.
-- src:1527 | Limitation
-- src:1528 | (3) A corporation may not indemnify an individual under subsection (1) unless the individual
-- src:1529 | (a) acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation, or, as the case may be, to the best interests of the other entity for which the individual acted as director or officer or in a similar capacity at the corporation’s request; and
-- src:1530 | (b) in the case of a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty, the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual’s conduct was lawful.
@ref CBCA s 124(3) (src:1527-1530)
GIVEN `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3) within s 124(3)` MEANS
        `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request`
    AND (   NOT `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty`
         OR `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`)

§§ `s 124(1) Indemnification`

-- src:1523 | Indemnification
-- src:1524 | 124 (1) A corporation may indemnify a director or officer of the corporation, a former director or officer of the corporation or another individual who acts or acted at the corporation’s request as a director or officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of another entity, against all costs, charges and expenses, including an amount paid to settle an action or satisfy a judgment, reasonably incurred by the individual in respect of any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or other proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association with the corporation or other entity.
@ref CBCA s 124(1) (src:1523-1524)
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)`
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may indemnify the individual within s 124(1)` MEANS
        NOT (`the position of the individual` EQUALS `none of those`)
    AND `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association`

§§ `s 124(2) Advance of costs`

-- src:1525 | Advance of costs
-- src:1526 | (2) A corporation may advance moneys to a director, officer or other individual for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection (1). The individual shall repay the moneys if the individual does not fulfil the conditions of subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 124(2) (src:1525-1526)
GIVEN `the moneys are for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may advance moneys within s 124(2)` MEANS
    `the moneys are for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection 124(1)`

-- src:1525 | Advance of costs
-- src:1526 | (2) A corporation may advance moneys to a director, officer or other individual for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection (1). The individual shall repay the moneys if the individual does not fulfil the conditions of subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 124(2) (src:1525-1526)
GIVEN `moneys were advanced to the individual under subsection 124(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual must repay the moneys within s 124(2)` MEANS
        `moneys were advanced to the individual under subsection 124(2)`
    AND (NOT `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3)`)

§§ `s 124(4) Indemnification in derivative actions`

-- Court approval is needed to indemnify, or advance moneys, in respect of an action by or on behalf of the
-- corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour, to which the individual is made a party
-- because of the association. The conditions of (3) must be fulfilled.
-- src:1531 | Indemnification in derivative actions
-- src:1532 | (4) A corporation may with the approval of a court, indemnify an individual referred to in subsection (1), or advance moneys under subsection (2), in respect of an action by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour, to which the individual is made a party because of the individual’s association with the corporation or other entity as described in subsection (1) against all costs, charges and expenses reasonably incurred by the individual in connection with such action, if the individual fulfils the conditions set out in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 124(4) (src:1531-1532)
GIVEN `the court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is made a party to the action because of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)`
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may with court approval indemnify or advance moneys in the derivative action within s 124(4)` MEANS
        `the court approves`
    AND `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour`
    AND `the individual is made a party to the action because of the association`
    AND NOT (`the position of the individual` EQUALS `none of those`)
    AND `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3) within s 124(3)`
            `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request`
            `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty`
            `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

-- The conditions together, for an indemnity under (1): subsection (3) must be fulfilled, and in a derivative
-- action subsection (4) governs (fork F-P10-15).
-- src:1523 | Indemnification
-- src:1524 | 124 (1) A corporation may indemnify a director or officer of the corporation, a former director or officer of the corporation or another individual who acts or acted at the corporation’s request as a director or officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of another entity, against all costs, charges and expenses, including an amount paid to settle an action or satisfy a judgment, reasonably incurred by the individual in respect of any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or other proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association with the corporation or other entity.
-- src:1525 | Advance of costs
-- src:1526 | (2) A corporation may advance moneys to a director, officer or other individual for the costs, charges and expenses of a proceeding referred to in subsection (1). The individual shall repay the moneys if the individual does not fulfil the conditions of subsection (3).
-- src:1527 | Limitation
-- src:1528 | (3) A corporation may not indemnify an individual under subsection (1) unless the individual
-- src:1529 | (a) acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation, or, as the case may be, to the best interests of the other entity for which the individual acted as director or officer or in a similar capacity at the corporation’s request; and
-- src:1530 | (b) in the case of a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty, the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual’s conduct was lawful.
-- src:1531 | Indemnification in derivative actions
-- src:1532 | (4) A corporation may with the approval of a court, indemnify an individual referred to in subsection (1), or advance moneys under subsection (2), in respect of an action by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour, to which the individual is made a party because of the individual’s association with the corporation or other entity as described in subsection (1) against all costs, charges and expenses reasonably incurred by the individual in connection with such action, if the individual fulfils the conditions set out in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 124(1) s 124(3) s 124(4) (src:1523-1524 src:1527-1532)
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)`
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may indemnify the individual within s 124(1), (3) and (4)` MEANS
        `the corporation may indemnify the individual within s 124(1)`
            `the position of the individual`
            `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in respect of a proceeding in which the individual is involved because of that association`
    AND `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3) within s 124(3)`
            `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request`
            `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty`
            `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`
    AND (   NOT `the action is by or on behalf of the corporation or other entity to procure a judgment in its favour`
         OR `the court approves`)

§§ `s 124(5) Right to indemnity`

-- src:1533 | Right to indemnity
-- src:1534 | (5) Despite subsection (1), an individual referred to in that subsection is entitled to indemnity from the corporation in respect of all costs, charges and expenses reasonably incurred by the individual in connection with the defence of any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or other proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the individual’s association with the corporation or other entity as described in subsection (1), if the individual seeking indemnity
-- src:1535 | (a) was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done; and
-- src:1536 | (b) fulfils the conditions set out in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 124(5) (src:1533-1536)
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)`
      `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in connection with the defence of a proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual is entitled to indemnity from the corporation within s 124(5)` MEANS
        NOT (`the position of the individual` EQUALS `none of those`)
    AND `the costs, charges and expenses were reasonably incurred in connection with the defence of a proceeding to which the individual is subject because of the association`
    AND `the individual was not judged by the court or other competent authority to have committed any fault or omitted to do anything that the individual ought to have done`
    AND `the individual fulfils the conditions of subsection 124(3) within s 124(3)`
            `the individual acted honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation or, as the case may be, of the other entity for which the individual acted at the corporation's request`
            `the proceeding is a criminal or administrative action or proceeding that is enforced by a monetary penalty`
            `the individual had reasonable grounds for believing that the individual's conduct was lawful`

§§ `s 124(6) Insurance`

-- src:1537 | Insurance
-- src:1538 | (6) A corporation may purchase and maintain insurance for the benefit of an individual referred to in subsection (1) against any liability incurred by the individual
-- src:1539 | (a) in the individual’s capacity as a director or officer of the corporation; or
-- src:1540 | (b) in the individual’s capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, if the individual acts or acted in that capacity at the corporation’s request.
@ref CBCA s 124(6) (src:1537-1540)
GIVEN `the position of the individual` IS A `Position of the individual under s 124(1)`
      `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, at the corporation's request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may purchase and maintain insurance within s 124(6)` MEANS
        NOT (`the position of the individual` EQUALS `none of those`)
    AND (   `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer of the corporation`
         OR `the liability is incurred in the individual's capacity as a director or officer, or similar capacity, of another entity, at the corporation's request`)

§§ `s 124(7) Application to court`

-- src:1541 | Application to court
-- src:1542 | (7) A corporation, an individual or an entity referred to in subsection (1) may apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity under this section and the court may so order and make any further order that it sees fit.
@ref CBCA s 124(7) (src:1541-1542)
GIVEN `the person is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an entity referred to in subsection 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity within s 124(7)` MEANS
        `the person is the corporation`
    OR  `the person is an individual referred to in subsection 124(1)`
    OR  `the person is an entity referred to in subsection 124(1)`

-- src:1541 | Application to court
-- src:1542 | (7) A corporation, an individual or an entity referred to in subsection (1) may apply to a court for an order approving an indemnity under this section and the court may so order and make any further order that it sees fit.
@ref CBCA s 124(7) (src:1541-1542)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may approve the indemnity and make any further order that it sees fit within s 124(7)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

§§ `s 124(8) Notice to Director`

-- src:1543 | Notice to Director
-- src:1544 | (8) An applicant under subsection (7) shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 124(8) (src:1543-1544)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 124(8)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

-- src:1543 | Notice to Director
-- src:1544 | (8) An applicant under subsection (7) shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 124(8) (src:1543-1544)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 124(8)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

§§ `s 124(9) Other notice`

-- src:1545 | Other notice
-- src:1546 | (9) On an application under subsection (7) the court may order notice to be given to any interested person and the person is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 124(9) (src:1545-1546)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order notice to be given to an interested person within s 124(9)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 124(7)`

-- src:1545 | Other notice
-- src:1546 | (9) On an application under subsection (7) the court may order notice to be given to any interested person and the person is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 124(9) (src:1545-1546)
GIVEN `the court has ordered notice to be given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the interested person is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 124(9)` MEANS
    `the court has ordered notice to be given to the person`

§ `s 125 Remuneration`

DECLARE `Person whose remuneration the directors may fix under s 125` IS ONE OF
    `a director of the corporation`
    `an officer of the corporation`
    `an employee of the corporation`
    `someone else`

-- src:1547 | Remuneration
-- src:1548 | 125 Subject to the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement, the directors of a corporation may fix the remuneration of the directors, officers and employees of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 125 (src:1547-1548)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person whose remuneration the directors may fix under s 125`
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may fix the remuneration within s 125` MEANS
        NOT (`the person` EQUALS `someone else`)
    AND (NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`)
